---
description: Never run zerollama/ollama/llama-server on the Proxmox hypervisor
alwaysApply: true
---

# PVE hypervisor — no inference serve

On **ryzen7950x0** (`/etc/pve` present, `systemd-detect-virt` is not `lxc`), do **not** start `zerollama serve`, `ollama serve`, or `llama-server`.

Production is **CT 1564** (`cudallama`, **`192.168.255.164:8080`**). Host `/root/zerollama` is a symlink into that CT’s private dir — running `~/bin/serve.sh` on the hypervisor still binds the **host** network, not the CT IP.

## Do this

```bash
pct exec 1564 -- ~/bin/serve.sh
# or
pct exec 1564 -- bash -lc 'screen -dmS ollama ~/bin/serve.sh'
curl -sS http://192.168.255.164:8080/api/version
```

## Do not

- `SCREEN -dmS ollama … /root/bin/serve.sh` on the hypervisor
- `kill` a PID just because `ps` shows `/root/zerollama/run/zerollama` — privileged LXC PIDs appear on the host; check cgroup `/lxc/1564` first
- Bind `:8080` / `:8081` / `:11434` on the PVE host

`serve_gpu_example.sh` / `serve_production_wrapper.sh` refuse to start when they detect the hypervisor (`ZEROLLAMA_ALLOW_PVE_HOST=1` override only for an explicit lab).
